ese cells  what we  noticed was after about 300 hours in  culture  a number of the wells we began to see  this deterioration and the drop off  in the total neurite length and i've  separated these wells out and  color coded them red so seven of the 24  wells we began to see this  this deterioration phenotype which we  weren't expecting  when we reviewed and looked at those  images and reanalyzed them for  confluence as well as neurite length  it was very clear that there was a  strong correlation between  the drop-off in neurites and this  increase in cell confluence  and it didn't take us long to by  retrospective analysis of the images  to verify that the reason why in the  subset of these wells we saw this  unstable neuron network  was because the non-terminal internally  differentiated precursors which were  relatively few and far between  had begun to proliferate and dominate  the culture  so we we throughout the course of the  assay had the ability to understand what  was going on so just to reflect on that  um example in this case continuous lyso  analysis provided us with two things one  was  a better biological insight than we feel  we would have had by an endpoint  approach  and secondly was a greater productivity  our real-time observation and management  measurement i'm sorry gave us a  verification of cell health and  morphology throughout the study  all of our measurements were made from  living non-perturbed cells we didn't  require to fix or stain or wash them  at all times understood the time course  of the neuro outgrowth and stabilization  and we could troubleshoot to identify  this precursor proliferation  complication with regards to  productivity  all of the images were automatically  taken by the inky site and automatically  analyzed so with no overhead to the  researcher  i showed you data from the 24 control  wells in this study  we took 78 time point measurements  equating to  just under 1900 data points these wells  uh took up no more than half a million  total sales which given these are  relatively expensive and pressure sales  was  an acceptable cost to us and we didn't  require to purchase any labeling  antibodies for the experiments  and importantly the all of the  measurements were non-exhaustive so the  cells were still viable at the end of  all this to do follow-on studies for  example things like immune scientific  chemistry  okay so let's think about the second  example this is slightly different  so um this is an example where  we assembled a co-culture assay to look  at  immune cell killing of adherent tumor  cells for an immuno oncology project  so briefly what we did is we created a  co-culture with ovarian cancer cells  with human peripheral blood blood  mononuclear cells pvmcs  as the effector cells we first labelled  the nuclei of the ovarian cancer cells  with  a nuclear targeted red fluorescent  protein  so that we could quantify the  cancer cells in their own right we  duplex this with a measurement of  apoptosis  using a fluorescent caspase-37 substrate  which  only fluoresces when cells begin to  express an active  caspase enzyme we activated the co  culture with il2 cd3 to  prompt the effector cells to target the  tumor cells we measured  the tumor cell  number and the apoptotic  cell death by quantifying the red and  green channels respectively  so to begin with how was continuous  lifestyle analysis applied well from the  outset when we grew these sculp3 target  cells  in six well plates we did the  transfection with the  uh knock light red lentivirus construct  at that point we didn't know what the  optimal concentration moi  of lentivirus to use so we did a simple  matrix experiment  where we used a range of different mois  in the absence and presence of polybrine  what you can see from this analysis in  the the right half of this  slide is the optimal concentration with  moi6  plus polybrine and after two days we saw  a high  infection rate and the cells the image  on the bottom left hand side  shows that roughly 70 to 80 percent of  these cells were expressing the the  nuclear targeted rfp  we then took these cells we continue  continued  to monitor them we put them into a t175  flask to bolt them  up and this now shows uh lifestyle  analysis  of the cells in this t flask and what  you can see here is the growth curve for  these cells  and an image taken at 100 hours showing  that now in the presence of the  pure mice and selecting antibiotic for  eliminating cells not expressing the rfp  we could purify the cell population  so we then progressed with this purified  cell population into plating these cells  in preparation for our co-culture assay  so we worked on 96 well plates and our  initial target  by seeding the skull cells at 2 000  cells per well  was uh to bring about roughly twenty  percent confluence  twenty percent area occupancy across  this plate  the data on the bottom left hand side of  this slide  shows we did a reasonably good job here  on average we had 18  confluence with relatively little  variance from  uh one well to the next and this sd  value of 2  was considered a good starting point and  you can see the image of those  healthy happy stocks resales on the  upper right hand panel  we then added the pbmcs so  we required 8 000 cells for well for  this experiment  and the yellow arrow highlights  uh one of these is this very small round  bright high contrast  cell contrasting obviously with the  larger red nucleated uh  skull three cells so the continuous y  cell analysis was used  basically to qc this plate before and  after the addition  of the effector cells  so moving on to the assay itself so  what you see here now is the continuous  monitoring of these cultures for a  further seven day period  and the top left-hand panel is the  microplate view so this analysis is done  in real time so you don't have to wait  to the end of seven days to  see the outcome of the experiment you're  watching what happens as time goes by  the parameter on the y-axis is the  number of red objects so the number of  living scof3 cells in the culture  and the controls are shown in the pink  and you can see  that as the skull cells proliferate over  time  after about 120 hours they are fully  confident  in the presence of pvmcs alone you see  no effect on the ability of the scots  resales to  proliferate but if you activate those  pvmcs with il2 cd3  which is now the blue line in the panel  on the top right  you can see that the cells stop  proliferating at around about 60 hours  and the cell number starts to  decrease as the effector cells start to  kill  the target cells if we look at the  green channel to monitor the  appearance of apoptotic skull 3 cells  in the control so the pink and the dark  blue  we saw little or no apoptosis up to  about 100 hours  after that as the cultures began to get  over confluent you start to see  some dying cells but a little  in the way of comparison with what you  see with the activated  bbmc so in the il-2cd3 group in the dark  blue  around about 60 hours we start to see  the appearance of  apoptotic tumor cells we can really  verify that that's happening by  inspecting the movie so this now shows a  movie  of these cells the red cells of the  tumor cells and you see the very highly  motile  pvmcs and in a moment you'll see one  particularly large  cell begins to degranulate having been  attacked by these tumor cells there it  goes  and then it glows green as the cascade  substrate  is cleaved and the fluorophore binds to  the dna  so we have a very visual method of  verifying uh  what we're trying to measure  okay and then finally for this story uh  we can do this at a scale  i show a full plate study here with inky  site zoom you could do actually six  plates and you could do six three eight  four world plates but the example here  is  four times 96 well plates this in fact  was an antibody dependent cell killing  assay  where we were looking to test the effect  of herceptin and  accepting via similars on uh  pvmc killing of tumor cells  the important values for the the  industrialists or the screeners in the  audience are  these play qcs their prime parameters  measured from the high and low controls  which were all in excess of 0.6  illustrating highly precise and robust  screening assays we required only a  small number of cells for the entire  study with 3 million pbmcs for the  entire study  and and i just show you one  representative concentration response  curve here for  accepting to illustrate how this  approach can be turned at scale  into robust quantitative pharmacology  okay and so just reflect on that example  too  so really similar high-level messages of  the value of the approach  biological insights and enhanced  productivity  we could monitor the full time course  using a direct readout so in this case  target cell death  throughout the course of this assay we  can multiplex that with the apoptosis  readout  and the cell morphology analysis to  really build confidence in the signals  that we were measuring  the time-lapse movies verify  certain physical interactions between  target effector cells and really  support and add credibility to the  quantified data  as with the previous example all of the  images were taken and analyzed  automatically by the inky site system  hopefully i showed you how we could  streamline some of the reagent and assay  build  using this continuous lifestyle analysis  approach  in the assay itself we had four 96 well  plates with two metric tricks and 64  time points so we analyze 49 000 data  points  in this study and again in similar ways  to that which i showed you before  the cells remain viable throughout the  experiment  for follow-on studies so you could lift  them to do flow cytometry analysis  or you could sample supernatants to  measure cytokines for example using  arises  okay so that's the story just to  wrap up i showed you to begin with  how the cellular 